// workiq-tierB-defender.kql
// =============================================================================
// Tier-B (telemetry) Work IQ invocation signal from Microsoft Defender XDR
// Advanced Hunting CloudAppEvents.
//
// Purpose:
//   Detect runtime invocations of the Work IQ MCP tool by Copilot Studio /
//   Copilot agents. This is the TELEMETRY tier. It must be joined with the
//   Tier-A configuration output (Get-WorkIqConfigState.ps1) before asserting
//   the canonical four-state observedstatus. Never treat a configuration signal
//   as an invocation, or vice-versa.
//
// Verified base query (do not alter the two filter lines):
//   CloudAppEvents
//   | where ActionType in ("ExecuteToolByGateway")
//   | where RawEventData contains "tool name"
//
//   "tool name" is a placeholder for the Work IQ MCP tool identifier. Set the
//   WorkIqToolToken parameter below to that identifier (preview: use-work-iq).
//
// Parameters:
//   LookbackDefender - time window (default 30d; the 30-day KPI lookback).
//   WorkIqToolToken  - the Work IQ MCP tool identifier to match in RawEventData.
//
// Output Schema:
//   Timestamp       (datetime) - event time
//   ToolName        (string)   - invoked tool identifier
//   AgentId         (string)   - invoking agent identifier (join key to Tier-A)
//   UserId          (string)   - invoking account (for business-user KPI)
//   AccountType     (string)   - account type, used to exclude service/test
//   TelemetrySource (string)   - constant "DefenderCloudAppEvents"
//
// Supports:
//   Control 3.2 (Primary)    - usage analytics / business impact reporting
//   Control 2.9 (Supporting) - agent performance / runtime monitoring
//   Control 2.24 (Supporting) - feature-enablement governance evidence
//
// Notes:
//   - CloudAppEvents requires Defender for Cloud Apps connected to Defender XDR.
//   - The Defender connector is in preview for some tenants at scaffold time;
//     verify availability before relying on it (build-time assumption).
//   - RawEventData is a dynamic JSON blob; the exact field paths used to extract
//     ToolName / AgentId / UserId are build-time assumptions and should be
//     validated against your tenant's payloads.
// =============================================================================

// Parameterized time range (KQL convention).
let LookbackDefender = 30d;
// Replace with the Work IQ MCP tool identifier. Preview default: use-work-iq.
// The verified base query used the literal placeholder "tool name".
let WorkIqToolToken = "tool name";
CloudAppEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(LookbackDefender)
| where ActionType in ("ExecuteToolByGateway")
| where RawEventData contains WorkIqToolToken
| extend Raw = todynamic(RawEventData)
| extend ToolName = tostring(Raw.ToolName)
| extend AgentId = tostring(coalesce(Raw.AgentId, Raw.BotId, Raw.AppId))
| extend UserId = tostring(coalesce(Raw.UserId, AccountId))
| project
    Timestamp,
    ToolName,
    AgentId,
    UserId,
    AccountType = tostring(AccountType),
    TelemetrySource = "DefenderCloudAppEvents"
| order by Timestamp desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tier-A posture companion (reference only -- not an invocation signal).
// Defender surfaces configured agent tools in AgentsInfo / AgentToolsDetails.
// NOTE: AgentsInfo was named AIAgentsInfo; the rename cutover is 2026-07-01.
// Use this only to corroborate Tier-A configuration, never to assert invocation.
//
//   let LookbackPosture = 30d;
//   AgentsInfo                     // was AIAgentsInfo before 2026-07-01
//   | where Timestamp > ago(LookbackPosture)
//   | join kind=leftouter AgentToolsDetails on $left.AgentId == $right.AgentId
//   | where ToolName has WorkIqToolToken
//   | project Timestamp, AgentId, ToolName
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
